1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,723
What would you say, if they threw you into a fire? He said:

2
00:00:03,773 --> 00:00:05,879
Allah is enough for us.

3
00:00:05,929 --> 00:00:09,939
They threw him into a blazing furnace. His crime?

4
00:00:10,050 --> 00:00:11,135
He told them:

5
00:00:11,185 --> 00:00:14,002
your Lord is the Lord of the heavens and the earth...

6
00:00:14,052 --> 00:00:16,309
and he broke their idols.

7
00:00:16,450 --> 00:00:17,468
But Allah said:

8
00:00:17,518 --> 00:00:21,521
"O fire, be coolness and safety upon Ibrahim."

9
00:00:22,034 --> 00:00:25,502
Who was this man, who stood alone against his father,

10
00:00:25,552 --> 00:00:27,617
his people, and a king?

11
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:32,064
Long ago, among a people devoted to statues,

12
00:00:32,114 --> 00:00:37,399
there lived a young man named Ibrahim, alayhis salaam.

13
00:00:37,449 --> 00:00:42,843
His people carved statues with their own hands, and stayed devoted to them.

14
00:00:42,966 --> 00:00:47,959
They called on them, hoping they would help, fearing they would harm.

15
00:00:48,100 --> 00:00:51,349
And his own father, Azar, worshipped them too.

16
00:00:51,559 --> 00:00:54,872
But the young man looked at the idols, and saw what they were:

17
00:00:54,922 --> 00:00:58,919
carved things that could not hear, and could not see.

18
00:00:59,222 --> 00:01:01,401
One day he said to his father:

19
00:01:01,451 --> 00:01:03,990
"Do you take idols as gods?

20
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:07,731
Indeed, I see you and your people in clear error."

21
00:01:07,872 --> 00:01:10,042
It was a dangerous thing to say.

22
00:01:10,092 --> 00:01:12,295
These idols were the way of their fathers,

23
00:01:12,345 --> 00:01:15,302
and the bond that held the whole people together.

24
00:01:15,512 --> 00:01:19,067
But Allah had given this young man his sound judgement,

25
00:01:19,117 --> 00:01:20,792
and a sound heart.

26
00:01:21,790 --> 00:01:26,533
Allah showed Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, the realm of the heavens and the earth,

27
00:01:26,583 --> 00:01:30,970
and gave him an argument against his people, step by step.

28
00:01:31,053 --> 00:01:34,242
When the night grew dark, he saw a star, and said:

29
00:01:34,292 --> 00:01:36,111
this is my lord.

30
00:01:36,161 --> 00:01:38,156
But when it set, he said:

31
00:01:38,239 --> 00:01:40,977
"I do not love those that disappear."

32
00:01:41,095 --> 00:01:43,120
Then he saw the moon rising, and said:

33
00:01:43,170 --> 00:01:44,518
this is my lord.

34
00:01:44,628 --> 00:01:46,102
But when it set, he said:

35
00:01:46,152 --> 00:01:47,464
unless my Lord guides me,

36
00:01:47,514 --> 00:01:50,775
I will surely be among those who go astray.

37
00:01:50,905 --> 00:01:52,985
Then he saw the sun rising.

38
00:01:53,046 --> 00:01:56,414
This is my lord, he said, this is greater.

39
00:01:56,529 --> 00:01:59,985
But when it set, he turned to his people and said:

40
00:02:00,126 --> 00:02:05,186
O my people, I am free from all that you associate with Allah.

41
00:02:05,397 --> 00:02:10,700
"Indeed, I have turned my face toward He who created the heavens and the earth,

42
00:02:10,750 --> 00:02:12,743
inclining toward truth,

43
00:02:12,793 --> 00:02:16,588
and I am not of those who associate others with Allah."

44
00:02:16,984 --> 00:02:20,283
Everything that rises... sets.

45
00:02:20,411 --> 00:02:24,196
Only the One who made them never disappears.

46
00:02:24,685 --> 00:02:26,349
But saying this aloud...

47
00:02:26,399 --> 00:02:30,724
was about to cost him his home, and nearly his life.

48
00:02:31,720 --> 00:02:35,211
The hardest call of all was to his own father.

49
00:02:35,261 --> 00:02:37,697
And listen to how gently he spoke.

50
00:02:37,838 --> 00:02:41,864
"O my father, why do you worship that which does not hear,

51
00:02:41,914 --> 00:02:45,534
and does not see, and will not benefit you at all?"

52
00:02:45,838 --> 00:02:46,844
O my father,

53
00:02:46,894 --> 00:02:50,211
knowledge has come to me that has not come to you.

54
00:02:50,261 --> 00:02:53,986
So follow me, and I will guide you to an even path.

55
00:02:54,127 --> 00:02:57,061
O my father, do not worship Satan.

56
00:02:57,111 --> 00:03:02,159
Indeed Satan has ever been, to the Most Merciful, disobedient.

57
00:03:02,370 --> 00:03:03,318
O my father,

58
00:03:03,368 --> 00:03:07,337
I fear that a punishment from the Most Merciful will touch you.

59
00:03:07,478 --> 00:03:09,439
Four times he called him:

60
00:03:09,522 --> 00:03:10,969
O my father.

61
00:03:11,019 --> 00:03:12,839
Every word, gentle.

62
00:03:12,889 --> 00:03:14,313
But his father answered:

63
00:03:14,363 --> 00:03:17,634
"Have you no desire for my gods, O Ibrahim?

64
00:03:17,684 --> 00:03:20,408
If you do not stop, I will surely stone you.

65
00:03:20,458 --> 00:03:23,185
So leave me, for a long time."

66
00:03:23,396 --> 00:03:25,842
And Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, said:

67
00:03:25,892 --> 00:03:27,595
"Peace be upon you.

68
00:03:27,645 --> 00:03:30,428
I will ask forgiveness for you from my Lord.

69
00:03:30,478 --> 00:03:33,460
Indeed, He is ever gracious to me."

70
00:03:34,460 --> 00:03:36,314
Words had not moved them.

71
00:03:36,364 --> 00:03:40,611
So Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, made a plan.

72
00:03:40,694 --> 00:03:42,072
He asked his people:

73
00:03:42,122 --> 00:03:46,692
"What are these statues to which you are devoted?" They said:

74
00:03:46,742 --> 00:03:49,678
we found our fathers worshipping them.

75
00:03:49,819 --> 00:03:50,885
He said:

76
00:03:50,968 --> 00:03:54,310
you and your fathers have been in clear error.

77
00:03:54,393 --> 00:03:55,597
And he swore:

78
00:03:55,647 --> 00:04:00,173
by Allah, I will plan against your idols after you turn your backs.

79
00:04:00,314 --> 00:04:02,725
He cast a look at the stars, and said:

80
00:04:02,775 --> 00:04:03,900
I am ill.

81
00:04:03,950 --> 00:04:06,349
So they turned away from him, and left.

82
00:04:06,399 --> 00:04:11,114
And Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, went to their gods alone.

83
00:04:11,255 --> 00:04:14,444
He broke the idols into pieces, all of them...

84
00:04:14,494 --> 00:04:16,235
except the biggest one.

85
00:04:16,538 --> 00:04:19,170
When the people returned, they cried:

86
00:04:19,220 --> 00:04:22,932
who has done this to our gods? Some said:

87
00:04:22,982 --> 00:04:25,138
we heard a young man speak of them.

88
00:04:25,188 --> 00:04:27,078
His name is Ibrahim.

89
00:04:27,161 --> 00:04:29,654
They brought him before everyone and asked:

90
00:04:29,704 --> 00:04:33,000
did you do this to our gods, O Ibrahim?

91
00:04:33,883 --> 00:04:34,576
He said:

92
00:04:34,626 --> 00:04:37,885
"Rather, this one, the biggest of them, did it.

93
00:04:37,935 --> 00:04:40,626
So ask them, if they can speak."

94
00:04:41,023 --> 00:04:43,879
For a moment, they turned on themselves:

95
00:04:43,936 --> 00:04:45,861
you are the wrongdoers!

96
00:04:45,972 --> 00:04:47,807
Then they turned back, and said:

97
00:04:47,857 --> 00:04:50,983
you know very well that these do not speak.

98
00:04:51,067 --> 00:04:52,027
And he said:

99
00:04:52,077 --> 00:04:54,836
then do you worship, instead of Allah,

100
00:04:54,886 --> 00:04:57,716
what can neither benefit you nor harm you?

101
00:04:57,766 --> 00:05:00,573
Shame on you, and on what you worship.

102
00:05:00,714 --> 00:05:02,884
Will you not use reason?

103
00:05:03,880 --> 00:05:06,061
They had lost the argument.

104
00:05:06,272 --> 00:05:08,487
So they turned to force.

105
00:05:08,628 --> 00:05:12,586
"Burn him, and support your gods, if you are to act."

106
00:05:12,727 --> 00:05:13,748
They said:

107
00:05:13,798 --> 00:05:18,087
build for him a furnace, and throw him into the blazing fire.

108
00:05:18,298 --> 00:05:22,058
A young man, alone, falling into the flames.

109
00:05:22,967 --> 00:05:26,121
And then Allah gave the fire a single command:

110
00:05:26,171 --> 00:05:30,662
"O fire, be coolness and safety upon Ibrahim."

111
00:05:30,803 --> 00:05:33,079
The fire that was made to burn...

112
00:05:33,129 --> 00:05:35,245
obeyed its Creator.

113
00:05:35,534 --> 00:05:39,993
And as they threw him, Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, had said:

114
00:05:40,043 --> 00:05:43,943
حَسْبُنَا اللّٰهُ وَنِعْمَ الْوَكِيْلُ.

115
00:05:43,993 --> 00:05:47,557
Allah is enough for us, and He is the best Guardian.

116
00:05:47,607 --> 00:05:52,400
"And they intended for him harm, but We made them the greatest losers."

117
00:05:52,541 --> 00:05:55,011
But the fire was not his hardest test.

118
00:05:55,061 --> 00:05:57,275
That one would come years later...

119
00:05:57,325 --> 00:05:58,658
in a dream.

120
00:05:59,660 --> 00:06:02,914
There was a king to whom Allah had given a kingdom.

121
00:06:02,964 --> 00:06:05,374
And because Allah had given him a kingdom,

122
00:06:05,424 --> 00:06:10,354
he argued with Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, about his Lord.

123
00:06:10,437 --> 00:06:13,661
Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, said:

124
00:06:13,711 --> 00:06:18,307
my Lord is the One who gives life and causes death.

125
00:06:18,390 --> 00:06:19,413
The king said:

126
00:06:19,463 --> 00:06:21,900
I give life and cause death.

127
00:06:22,910 --> 00:06:26,368
So Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, said:

128
00:06:26,451 --> 00:06:30,023
"Indeed, Allah brings up the sun from the east,

129
00:06:30,073 --> 00:06:32,684
so bring it up from the west."

130
00:06:33,196 --> 00:06:35,364
And the disbeliever was overwhelmed.

131
00:06:35,414 --> 00:06:37,640
A king, with all his kingdom...

132
00:06:37,690 --> 00:06:39,747
silenced by one sentence.

133
00:06:39,797 --> 00:06:42,996
And Allah does not guide the wrongdoing people.

134
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:46,184
His father had threatened to stone him.

135
00:06:46,234 --> 00:06:48,213
His people had tried to burn him.

136
00:06:48,263 --> 00:06:51,250
A king had argued against his Lord.

137
00:06:51,461 --> 00:06:53,601
And one man believed in him:

138
00:06:53,679 --> 00:06:56,766
Lut, alayhis salaam.

139
00:06:56,816 --> 00:07:00,691
So Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, left his people,

140
00:07:00,741 --> 00:07:05,381
and Allah brought him and Lut to a land He had blessed.

141
00:07:05,431 --> 00:07:06,171
He said:

142
00:07:06,221 --> 00:07:08,563
"Indeed, I will go to my Lord.

143
00:07:08,613 --> 00:07:10,121
He will guide me."

144
00:07:10,262 --> 00:07:11,171
He said:

145
00:07:11,221 --> 00:07:14,065
I will leave you and what you worship besides Allah,

146
00:07:14,115 --> 00:07:16,542
and I will call upon my Lord.

147
00:07:16,626 --> 00:07:19,977
And as he grew older, he made one more dua:

148
00:07:20,027 --> 00:07:24,111
"My Lord, grant me a child from among the righteous."

149
00:07:24,161 --> 00:07:26,061
And Allah gave him good news:

150
00:07:26,111 --> 00:07:27,839
a forbearing boy.

151
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:32,611
His son Ismail, alayhis salaam, was born.

152
00:07:32,753 --> 00:07:35,909
And then came a test that no father would choose.

153
00:07:36,050 --> 00:07:42,513
By Allah's command, Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, brought the baby and his mother to a dry valley,

154
00:07:42,563 --> 00:07:45,917
with no water, no plants, and no people.

155
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,914
The valley of Makkah.

156
00:07:47,997 --> 00:07:49,015
He left them there,

157
00:07:49,065 --> 00:07:52,145
with a bag of dates and a skin of water.

158
00:07:52,334 --> 00:07:55,109
As he walked away, the mother called after him:

159
00:07:55,159 --> 00:07:59,112
has Allah commanded you to do this? He said: yes.

160
00:07:59,162 --> 00:08:00,136
And she said:

161
00:08:00,186 --> 00:08:02,977
then He will not neglect us.

162
00:08:03,176 --> 00:08:06,615
Out of their sight, Ibrahim, alayhis salaam,

163
00:08:06,665 --> 00:08:09,791
faced the House, raised his hands, and prayed:

164
00:08:09,862 --> 00:08:16,249
"Our Lord, I have settled some of my descendants in an uncultivated valley near Your sacred House,

165
00:08:16,299 --> 00:08:18,866
that they may establish prayer."

166
00:08:19,077 --> 00:08:22,998
When the water ran out, the mother ran between two hills,

167
00:08:23,048 --> 00:08:28,154
Safa and Marwa, seven times, searching for any sign of help.

168
00:08:29,084 --> 00:08:30,778
Then she heard a voice.

169
00:08:30,828 --> 00:08:35,643
At the place of Zamzam, the ground was struck, and water flowed.

170
00:08:35,943 --> 00:08:38,422
The spring of Zamzam.

171
00:08:38,472 --> 00:08:40,987
It is still flowing today.

172
00:08:41,037 --> 00:08:44,819
Every pilgrim who walks between Safa and Marwa is

173
00:08:44,869 --> 00:08:48,327
walking in the footsteps of a mother who trusted Allah.

174
00:08:48,468 --> 00:08:50,556
And that baby would grow up...

175
00:08:50,639 --> 00:08:53,621
to become the son in his father's dream.

176
00:08:54,620 --> 00:08:58,988
Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, had seen the fire turn cool.

177
00:08:59,038 --> 00:09:01,872
He had seen his Lord answer his duas.

178
00:09:01,935 --> 00:09:05,540
And still, he asked his Lord for one more thing.

179
00:09:05,844 --> 00:09:09,172
"My Lord, show me how You give life to the dead."

180
00:09:09,222 --> 00:09:10,217
Allah said:

181
00:09:10,267 --> 00:09:12,051
have you not believed? He said:

182
00:09:12,101 --> 00:09:15,767
"Yes, but only that my heart may be satisfied."

183
00:09:15,817 --> 00:09:17,599
So Allah told him:

184
00:09:17,765 --> 00:09:20,575
take four birds, and draw them close to you.

185
00:09:20,625 --> 00:09:23,265
Then put a portion of them on each hill.

186
00:09:23,315 --> 00:09:25,242
Then call them.

187
00:09:25,292 --> 00:09:29,094
Call them, Allah said, and they will come to you in haste.

188
00:09:29,144 --> 00:09:33,382
And know that Allah is Exalted in Might, and Wise.

189
00:09:33,523 --> 00:09:35,946
Faith does not mean you never ask.

190
00:09:35,996 --> 00:09:39,373
It means you ask the One who has the answer.

191
00:09:40,370 --> 00:09:41,655
Years passed.

192
00:09:41,705 --> 00:09:44,105
Ismail, alayhis salaam,

193
00:09:44,155 --> 00:09:48,379
grew into a boy who could walk and work beside his father.

194
00:09:48,590 --> 00:09:52,348
Then Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, saw a dream.

195
00:09:52,453 --> 00:09:55,818
And his son understood it as a command from Allah.

196
00:09:55,868 --> 00:09:56,666
He said:

197
00:09:56,716 --> 00:09:58,012
"O my son,

198
00:09:58,062 --> 00:10:01,797
indeed I have seen in a dream that I sacrifice you.

199
00:10:01,847 --> 00:10:03,562
So see what you think."

200
00:10:03,612 --> 00:10:05,066
And the son answered:

201
00:10:05,116 --> 00:10:08,321
"O my father, do as you are commanded.

202
00:10:08,371 --> 00:10:12,912
You will find me, if Allah wills, of the steadfast."

203
00:10:13,054 --> 00:10:15,663
When they had both submitted, and Ibrahim,

204
00:10:15,713 --> 00:10:19,856
alayhis salaam, laid him down on his forehead...

205
00:10:20,881 --> 00:10:22,435
Allah called to him:

206
00:10:22,485 --> 00:10:25,321
O Ibrahim, you have fulfilled the vision.

207
00:10:25,378 --> 00:10:26,824
And Allah says:

208
00:10:26,874 --> 00:10:30,111
indeed, this was the clear trial.

209
00:10:30,194 --> 00:10:33,826
"And We ransomed him with a great sacrifice."

210
00:10:34,130 --> 00:10:38,190
Every Eid al-Adha, Muslims remember this moment:

211
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:41,960
a father and a son who both submitted to Allah.

212
00:10:42,960 --> 00:10:46,878
Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, was now an old man.

213
00:10:46,928 --> 00:10:52,330
And his wife, Sarah, alayhas salaam, had never had a child.

214
00:10:52,448 --> 00:10:54,675
One day, guests entered upon him.

215
00:10:54,725 --> 00:11:00,698
Strangers, a people unknown. They said: peace. He said: peace.

216
00:11:00,816 --> 00:11:04,749
Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, did not delay.

217
00:11:04,799 --> 00:11:09,386
He went to his family, and came back with a fat roasted calf.

218
00:11:09,527 --> 00:11:11,485
He placed it near them and said:

219
00:11:11,535 --> 00:11:15,642
"Will you not eat?" But their hands did not reach for it.

220
00:11:15,692 --> 00:11:17,513
And he felt afraid of them.

221
00:11:17,654 --> 00:11:18,150
They said:

222
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:19,753
do not fear.

223
00:11:19,895 --> 00:11:23,269
We are messengers, sent to the people of Lut.

224
00:11:23,319 --> 00:11:25,719
And they gave him good news.

225
00:11:25,769 --> 00:11:29,039
His wife, who was standing nearby, smiled.

226
00:11:29,089 --> 00:11:31,245
And they gave her the good news of a son,

227
00:11:31,295 --> 00:11:36,146
Ishaq, and after Ishaq, Yaqub, alayhimus salaam.

228
00:11:36,287 --> 00:11:37,131
She said:

229
00:11:37,181 --> 00:11:39,523
shall I give birth, when I am an old woman,

230
00:11:39,573 --> 00:11:42,053
and my husband is an old man?

231
00:11:42,103 --> 00:11:45,432
This is an amazing thing! They said:

232
00:11:45,482 --> 00:11:48,485
"Are you amazed at the decree of Allah?

233
00:11:48,535 --> 00:11:52,224
May the mercy of Allah and His blessings be upon you,

234
00:11:52,274 --> 00:11:53,909
people of the house."

235
00:11:54,050 --> 00:11:59,934
From Ismail, alayhis salaam, would come the Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him.

236
00:12:00,061 --> 00:12:03,334
From Ishaq, alayhis salaam, would come Yaqub,

237
00:12:03,384 --> 00:12:10,100
Yusuf, Musa, Dawud, Sulaiman and Isa, alayhimus salaam.

238
00:12:10,226 --> 00:12:14,980
And Allah placed prophethood and the Book among his descendants.

239
00:12:15,980 --> 00:12:20,539
Then Allah showed Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, the place of His House.

240
00:12:20,589 --> 00:12:23,710
And father and son began to build.

241
00:12:23,828 --> 00:12:27,714
Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, laid the stones.

242
00:12:27,764 --> 00:12:30,918
Ismail, alayhis salaam, carried them.

243
00:12:30,968 --> 00:12:34,577
And as the walls of the Kaaba rose, they prayed:

244
00:12:34,649 --> 00:12:37,292
"Our Lord, accept this from us.

245
00:12:37,342 --> 00:12:40,684
Indeed, You are the Hearing, the Knowing."

246
00:12:40,964 --> 00:12:43,503
Our Lord, make us Muslims to You,

247
00:12:43,553 --> 00:12:46,489
and from our descendants a Muslim nation.

248
00:12:46,572 --> 00:12:50,169
Show us our rites, and accept our repentance.

249
00:12:50,473 --> 00:12:52,938
And they asked for one more thing:

250
00:12:53,129 --> 00:12:57,142
our Lord, send among them a messenger from themselves,

251
00:12:57,192 --> 00:12:59,825
who will recite Your verses to them.

252
00:13:00,016 --> 00:13:02,823
Long after, Allah answered that dua:

253
00:13:02,873 --> 00:13:06,443
Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him.

254
00:13:06,514 --> 00:13:08,264
Then Allah commanded:

255
00:13:08,314 --> 00:13:10,946
"Proclaim to the people the Hajj.

256
00:13:10,996 --> 00:13:13,012
They will come to you on foot,

257
00:13:13,062 --> 00:13:17,135
and on every lean camel, from every distant pass."

258
00:13:17,277 --> 00:13:18,780
And they still come.

259
00:13:19,043 --> 00:13:24,037
Millions every year, just as Allah promised Ibrahim, alayhis salaam.

260
00:13:25,040 --> 00:13:31,027
In his old age, Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, stood in the valley that had once been empty,

261
00:13:31,077 --> 00:13:35,743
and he made a dua that Muslims still recite today.

262
00:13:35,873 --> 00:13:38,772
"My Lord, make this city secure,

263
00:13:38,822 --> 00:13:42,953
and keep me and my sons away from worshipping idols."

264
00:13:43,025 --> 00:13:44,414
Praise be to Allah,

265
00:13:44,464 --> 00:13:48,082
who gave me in my old age Ismail and Ishaq.

266
00:13:48,255 --> 00:13:52,345
Indeed, my Lord is the Hearer of supplication.

267
00:13:52,405 --> 00:13:57,756
"My Lord, make me one who establishes prayer, and from my descendants too.

268
00:13:57,873 --> 00:14:00,610
Our Lord, and accept my dua."

269
00:14:00,660 --> 00:14:03,547
"Our Lord, forgive me, and my parents,

270
00:14:03,597 --> 00:14:07,612
and the believers, on the Day the account is established."

271
00:14:07,823 --> 00:14:10,861
And Muslims still make this dua today.

272
00:14:10,989 --> 00:14:13,745
The words of Ibrahim, alayhis salaam,

273
00:14:13,795 --> 00:14:16,913
kept in the Quran, still on our tongues.

274
00:14:17,910 --> 00:14:20,987
A young man among idols who would not bow.

275
00:14:21,037 --> 00:14:24,613
A son who spoke gently to a father who threatened him.

276
00:14:24,663 --> 00:14:26,499
A young man in the fire.

277
00:14:26,549 --> 00:14:28,606
A father in a dry valley.

278
00:14:28,656 --> 00:14:34,065
A father and son raising the foundations of a House for all people.

279
00:14:34,115 --> 00:14:36,502
Every time, he turned to Allah.

280
00:14:36,552 --> 00:14:39,655
And every time, Allah was enough for him.

281
00:14:39,773 --> 00:14:40,848
Allah says:

282
00:14:40,898 --> 00:14:42,449
"There has already been for you an

283
00:14:42,499 --> 00:14:46,073
excellent pattern in Abraham and those with him."

284
00:14:46,191 --> 00:14:48,817
And Allah kept his name with ours:

285
00:14:48,867 --> 00:14:52,831
every time we send blessings on the Prophet, peace be upon him,

286
00:14:52,881 --> 00:14:57,581
as he taught us, we name Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim.

287
00:14:57,631 --> 00:15:00,020
"Peace upon Ibrahim."

288
00:15:00,070 --> 00:15:01,408
So when you feel alone,

289
00:15:01,458 --> 00:15:04,246
say what he said as they threw him into the fire:

290
00:15:04,296 --> 00:15:08,088
حَسْبُنَا اللّٰهُ وَنِعْمَ الْوَكِيْلُ.

291
00:15:08,138 --> 00:15:12,050
Allah is enough for us, and He is the best Guardian.

292
00:15:12,121 --> 00:15:15,023
Which moment of his story moved you most?

293
00:15:15,216 --> 00:15:16,793
Tell us in the comments.

294
00:15:16,843 --> 00:15:25,131
And watch the full movies of Prophet Musa and Prophet Sulaiman, alayhimas salaam... links below.
